/**
 * ROUND 75 -- models packed from ONE drawn view, mirrored into the eight
 * isometric columns rather than drawn eight times.
 *
 * Four of the eight facings are the artist's own view and four are its
 * horizontal mirror, which is a real second view (east and west genuinely are
 * mirrors in this projection -- it is the same trick round 32's armoured
 * player uses). The four that are NOT mirrors -- north, south and the two
 * remaining diagonals -- show the same face as their nearest neighbour.
 *
 * Listed rather than left to be discovered: these are the models to re-request
 * with rotations, and until then this is what "the door is on the wrong side"
 * will mean when someone notices it.
 *
 * `armorsmith` is not mirrored at all: its shopfront carries a painted sign
 * reading FORGE & SHIELD, and a mirrored sign is mirror-writing. It uses its
 * native view in all eight columns.
 */
